   "notes": [
    "datashader is excluded from the histogram chart (unsupported): datashader has no 1-D histogram: the bin counts would come from numpy, so the timing would not measure datashader.",
    "Mosaic bins with vg.bin({steps}) treat steps as a niced maximum, not an exact count: for this data span it renders ~92 bins where other tools render exactly `bins`; the query cost is equivalent (one GROUP BY over the data).",
    "Vaex reads the shared Parquet input like every disk tool \u2014 a cross-tool input-format constraint, not vaex's optimal native format (vaex's docs recommend HDF5 and note a decompression penalty for Parquet).",
    "Multi-trace histograms are not pixel-identical across tools: flexviz bins every trace over the shared x-axis range (union of extents); Mosaic and Vaex bin each trace over its own column extent. Per-trace counts sum to rows either way and the scan cost is equivalent.",
    "mosaic-server on a disk source is loaded as a VIEW over the file, so the scan stays inside the timed window. This is a disclosed deviation from Mosaic's loadParquet default, which materializes a table before any query runs; the in-memory cells do use that materializing default.",
    "Vaex in-memory histogram timings can be dominated by fixed Matplotlib/PNG/browser overhead at these output sizes.",
    "mosaic-wasm compute in the browser and are benchmarked in-memory ONLY: the disk cells are out of scope by benchmark design, not because the engines lack a file path. Those cells are recorded as source_out_of_scope, never as failures.",
    "mosaic-wasm lets DuckDB-WASM pick its own build: selectBundle() feature detection over the vendored `mvp` and `eh` candidates \u2014 the documented default path, single-threaded. The experimental COI/pthreads build is not vendored (it needs cross-origin isolation, which changes the page's capabilities). The selected bundle is recorded per run.",
    "perspective-server is excluded from the histogram chart (unsupported): perspective has no histogram chart type: viewer-charts 5.2 ships no binning at all and \"Density\" is a 2-D radial-splat KDE, a different trace type (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-22-perspective5-gate.md).",
    "perspective-wasm is excluded from the histogram chart (unsupported): perspective has no histogram chart type: viewer-charts 5.2 ships no binning at all and \"Density\" is a 2-D radial-splat KDE, a different trace type (docs/superpowers/specs/2026-08-22-perspective5-gate.md)."
   ]
